KEY: the estimand is the MEAN held-out joint loss over INDEPENDENT (ROI split, model
     seed) draws -- that is the quantity CRC Theorem 2.1 bounds. A single run's loss
     above alpha refutes nothing, and no cell here is labelled a voided certificate.
     'sel.stat' is the calibration selection statistic, <= alpha by construction whenever
     a threshold was feasible, so it can never show a failure on its own.
     READ EVERY LOSS WITH ITS COVERAGE: a joint mass goes to 0 by abstaining.
     'paired vs Mondrian' is computed only on runs where BOTH arms certified.
     Temperature is fitted on ROIs DISJOINT from the CRC calibration ROIs.
     dropB10 / dropB1B9B10 isolate band loss; L2A_real is an OPERATIONAL L1C->L2A domain
     shift (BOA reflectance, atmospheric correction, B10 absent) -- do not attribute the
     clean->L2A_real difference to band loss alone.

